AWS Security Services: KMS, GuardDuty, WAF & Shield Explained

Security is one of the most critical pillars of cloud architecture.
AWS provides powerful, managed services that help you secure your applications, data, and infrastructure — without building everything from scratch.

Today, let’s break down four key AWS security services that every engineer and interviewer expects you to know


🔹 1️⃣ AWS KMS (Key Management Service)

AWS KMS is a fully managed service for creating, managing, and controlling encryption keys.

💡 What KMS Does:

Encrypts data stored in S3, EBS, RDS, DynamoDB, Lambda, and more

Provides Customer Managed Keys (CMK)

Integrates with IAM for granular access control

Supports automatic key rotation

Logs all key usage via CloudTrail


📍 Use Cases:

Encrypting sensitive data

Managing secure access to encryption keys

Compliance requirements (HIPAA, PCI, GDPR)


🔹 2️⃣ Amazon GuardDuty

GuardDuty is AWS’s threat detection service powered by ML and threat intelligence.

💡 What GuardDuty Detects:

Unusual IAM activity

Compromised EC2 instances

Malicious IP/domain communication

Suspicious S3 access

Crypto mining attempts

Reconnaissance activities


📍 Use Cases:

Continuous monitoring

Early security threat detection

Security operations (SOC) automation



🔹 3️⃣ AWS WAF (Web Application Firewall)

AWS WAF protects your applications from common web exploits like:

SQL injection

Cross-site scripting (XSS)

Bad bots

Layer 7 DDoS attacks


💡 Features:

Managed rule sets

Custom rules (IP blocks, regex, geolocation)

Integrates with CloudFront, ALB, API Gateway


📍 Use Cases:

Protect APIs & websites

Block malicious traffic

Rate limiting



🔹 4️⃣ AWS Shield (DDoS Protection)

🛡 Shield Standard:

Free for all AWS customers

Protects against common Layer 3 & 4 DDoS attacks


🛡 Shield Advanced:

Additional protection for mission-critical apps

24×7 AWS DDoS response team (DRT)

Cost protection against scaling spikes

Global threat visibility


📍 Use Cases:

Large-scale applications

High-availability architectures

Financial / e-commerce platforms


🔍 Quick Comparison (Interview Cheat Sheet)

Service	Purpose

KMS	Encryption key management
GuardDuty	Threat detection & monitoring
WAF	Protects web apps from Layer 7 attacks
Shield	Protects apps from DDoS attacks



